      "message": "I was just thinking of creating some inlines such as:\n```\nstatic inline void\n__trace_irq_enable_rcuidle(unsigned long a0, unsigned long a1)\n{\n        trace_irq_enable_rcuidle(a0, a1);\n        trace_android_rvh_irqs_enable(a0, a1);\n}\n```\nThen modify the `trace(point)` macro to point to these with the vendor hook inside.\n```\n#define trace(point)\tif (!in_nmi()) __trace_##point##_rcuidle\n```\n\nHowever, we would need 8 of these so it might be too verbose. I was hoping to get rid of the duplicated `if (!in_nmi())` branch already included with the `trace()` macro. I suppose further macro magic can be done to avoid this but it\u0027s not worth it.",
